      "next_deadline": "No application process. Requests are taken to the Board through Human Services Agency or Behavioral Health Services sponsorship.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "San Joaquin County has no county housing trust fund, no county housing bond and no inclusionary ordinance; the County's own capital for multifamily is limited to HUD pass-through funds administered by the Human Services Agency Neighborhood Preservation Division (sjchsa.org), while the regional gap lender is the SJCOG-sponsored San Joaquin Regional Housing Fund and the main voucher and development partner is the Housing Authority of the County of San Joaquin (HACSJ). Recorded so the gap is explicit: County General Fund money for multifamily has been rare and discretionary, and the County's 2026 posture is to route capital through the SJCOG Regional Housing Fund (which the County helped capitalize through Measure K) and operating dollars through BHSA, HHAP and PLHA. Mountain House, incorporated in 2024, holds an $8.19 million affordable housing fund from its community services district era (Housing Element), now a city program for Pass 3.",
